  "id": "abidat_rma",
  "name": "ʿAbidat rma (Chaouia hunters' troupe song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung and danced art of the hunters' guilds of central Morocco (the Chaouia, Ourdigha and Tadla plains around Khouribga, Oued Zem and Beni Mellal), historically performed to serve and entertain hunting parties. A troupe led by a mqaddem sings poetry in chorus to bendir frame drums and taarija clay drums, with the beat marked by a large pair of shears (mqass) struck with an iron rod, which has no card; dancers add broad cadenced movements, stamping and synchronised clapping. Troupes appear at the national Abidat Rma festival in Khouribga and on Moroccan radio-television.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ʿabidat rma, hunting Song. single lead single track no stacking. juniper bent frame canonical Maghrebi bendir, taarija, hand clap. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
